.TH RUNNERDECK 1 "2026-11-16" "RunnerDeck" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
runnerdeck \- manage a pool of self-hosted GitHub Actions runners
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B runnerdeck
[\fIcommand\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
RunnerDeck runs a pool of self-hosted GitHub Actions runners on this machine.
With no command it starts the dashboard on http://127.0.0.1:8090. The other
commands manage the same pool from a terminal, without the dashboard running.
.SH RUNNER COMMANDS
.TP
.B list, ls [--watch]
Show the runners on this machine.
.TP
.B status [--watch]
Like list, with what GitHub reports for each runner.
.TP
.B start \fIrunner...\fR | --all
Start runners.
.TP
.B stop \fIrunner...\fR | --all
Stop runners. Refuses if a runner is running a job, unless --force is given.
.TP
.B restart \fIrunner...\fR
Stop, then start, runners.
.TP
.B rolling-restart \fIrunner...\fR | --all
Wait for each runner to be idle, then restart it, one at a time.
.TP
.B drain \fIrunner...\fR | --all
Wait until idle, then stop the runners and clear their work folders.
.TP
.B add [--name \fIN\fR] [--ephemeral] [--label \fIL\fR]
Add and start a new runner.
.TP
.B delete, rm \fIrunner...\fR
Stop, deregister and remove runners.
.TP
.B rename \fIrunner\fR \fIname\fR
Re-register a runner under a new name.
.TP
.B force-idle \fIrunner\fR
Clear a stuck busy state on GitHub for a runner that is stopped here.
.TP
.B resize \fIcount\fR
Make the pool runner-base plus \fIcount\fR runners (1 to 30).
.TP
.B maintenance on|off|status
Drain every runner and refuse new starts, or lift that.
.TP
.B logs \fIrunner\fR [-n \fIN\fR] [-f]
Show a runner's log. -f follows it.
.SH SETUP COMMANDS
.TP
.B setup [--scope org|repo] [--org \fIO\fR | --repo \fIOWNER/REPO\fR]
Choose what RunnerDeck manages. Asks for anything not given.
.TP
.B config list|get|set|unset
Read and change settings. "config list --all" shows every name.
.TP
.B auth status|login|totp
Check or start the GitHub sign-in; set up the dashboard TOTP login.
.TP
.B doctor
Check this machine's setup.
.SH PROGRAM COMMANDS
.TP
.B run [--open] [\fIPORT\fR]
Start the dashboard.
.TP
.B update [--check] [--yes]
Upgrade to the latest release the way this copy was installed.
Other commands, in a terminal, also name a newer release and the link to it.
Set RUNNERDECK_NO_UPDATE_NOTICE=1 to hide that line.
.TP
.B install [--dir \fIDIR\fR], uninstall
Link the checkout's runnerdeck script onto your PATH, or remove the link.
Only for a source checkout.
.TP
.B completion bash|zsh|fish|powershell
Print a shell completion script.
.TP
.B version, --version, -v
Print the version.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --json
Machine-readable output.
.TP
.B --force
Do not check GitHub for a running job first. This can interrupt a job.
.TP
.B --timeout \fISECONDS\fR
How long drain, rolling-restart and maintenance wait for a job to finish.
.TP
.B -y, --yes
Do not ask before updating.
.TP
.B -q, --quiet
Print only errors.
.TP
.B --no-color
Turn colour off. NO_COLOR=1 does the same.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 if the command failed or was refused.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/runnerdeck
Settings, history and runners. On macOS the default is ~/.runnerdeck.
.TP
.I ~/.config/runnerdeck/pool-dir
Pool directory saved by "runnerdeck config set pool-dir". The launcher reads
this before it creates the default data directory.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/AnikethTS/RunnerDeck
